y in production. After the rollback, the service is healthy in all regions and the error rate is 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before it was promoted. Follow-up needed: find the root cause in v2.3.1 and review why it was promoted after failing in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15070, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Kwamzszkrue7s7GFUGnJ83", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 15070, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Kwamzszkrue7s7GFUGnJ83", "kind": "garbled", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 16480, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Wc6Mw2qe6fXFN85rM9SSuP", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 16780, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Wc6Mw2qe6fXFN85rM9SSuP", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16780, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Wc6Mw2qe6fXFN85rM9SSuP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20842, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production (v2.2.9 is older).\n- **After:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n\n**Incident INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api)**\n- It says what failed, which version we rolled back to, and the health and error rate afterwards.\n- Opening it returned a \"502 Bad Gateway\" error, but the incident list shows it was created. To avoid paging on-call twice, I didn't send it again, so there's only one incident.\n- It lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.\n  - Find out why it was promoted even though its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NEyPw6R7upza7qUt7hg1gN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01X6NvzeJUyrSEXBodqnBcfd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UhvR6bTNEGnFwxBJ8zgMLw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017xMDBjdqDETaoUsodpRiKM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CXK5u5hAjL6omqJ7eRzdnK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Kwamzszkrue7s7GFUGnJ83", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. We rolled back all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, the service is healthy in all regions and the error rate is 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before it was promoted. Follow-up needed: find the root cause in v2.3.1 and review why it was promoted after failing in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Wc6Mw2qe6fXFN85rM9SSuP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production (v2.2.9 is older).\n- **After:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n\n**Incident INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api)**\n- It says what failed, which version we rolled back to, and the health and error rate afterwards.\n- Opening it returned a \"502 Bad Gateway\" error, but the incident list shows it was created. To avoid paging on-call twice, I didn't send it again, so there's only one incident.\n- It lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.\n  - Find out why it was promoted even though its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}